---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import Wobbly from "../components/Wobbly.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config";
import { getIcon } from "../data/icons";
import { DEFAULTS } from "../lib/settings";
import { snippet } from "../lib/snippets";
import { highlightHtml } from "../lib/highlight";

const heart = getIcon("heart");
const inline = snippet("svg", heart, DEFAULTS).replace(/d="[^"]+"/, 'd="M12.16 19.38Q11.91 19.43…"');
const sprite = `<svg width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
     stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
  <use href="/sprite.svg#heart" />
</svg>`;
const img = `<img src="/svg/heart.svg" width="24" height="24" alt="Favourite" />`;
const packages = [
  { name: "zicons-react", code: `import { PencilIcon } from "zicons-react";

<PencilIcon size={32} color="#ff4757" />
<PencilIcon boil />
<PencilIcon boil="hover" />` },
  { name: "zicons-vue", code: `import { PencilIcon } from "zicons-vue";

<PencilIcon :size="32" color="#ff4757" />
<PencilIcon boil />
<PencilIcon boil="hover" />` },
  { name: "zicons-svelte", code: `import { PencilIcon } from "zicons-svelte";

<PencilIcon size={32} color="#ff4757" />
<PencilIcon boil />
<PencilIcon boil="hover" />` },
  { name: "zicons", code: `import { pencil, toSvg } from "zicons";

el.innerHTML = toSvg(pencil, { size: 32, boil: "hover" });` },
];
const wobbleTag = `<script src="${SITE.url}/wobble/v1.js"></script>

<svg class="zi-boil-sm" …>…</svg>
<svg class="zi-boil" …>…</svg>`;
const wobbleOpts = `<script src="${SITE.url}/wobble/v1.js" data-respect-reduced-motion></script>`;
const wobbleManual = `<script src="${SITE.url}/wobble/v1.js" data-manual></script>
<script>
  zicons.wobble({ respectReducedMotion: true });
</script>`;
---

<Base title="Using the icons · zicons" description="How to use zicons as inline SVG, a sprite, an image, or with the wobble helper.">
  <article class="prose-sk pt-10">
    <span class="tape">using them</span>
    <Wobbly text="put them anywhere" tag="h1" class="mt-4 text-[clamp(2.6rem,7vw,4.6rem)]" />
    <p class="mt-6">
      Every icon is one small SVG. Open an icon, set the colour, size and stroke you like, and copy it in the format you
      need. A few things aren't obvious, so they're here.
    </p>

    <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
    <p>
      There's a package for React, Vue and Svelte, plus <code>zicons</code> for plain JavaScript. Each icon is its
      own import, so only the ones you use end up in your bundle. They all take <code>size</code>,
      <code>color</code>, <code>strokeWidth</code> and <code>boil</code>: <code>boil</code> makes the line wobble,
      and <code>boil="hover"</code> wobbles only on hover or focus.
    </p>
    {
      packages.map((p) => (
        <>
          <p class="pkg"><code>npm i {p.name}</code></p>
          <pre class="code" set:html={highlightHtml(p.code)} />
        </>
      ))
    }

    <h2>Inline SVG</h2>
    <p>
      Paste the SVG straight into your HTML. With the default <code>stroke="currentColor"</code> the icon takes the
      colour of the text around it, so <code>color: tomato</code> on a parent turns it tomato.
    </p>
    <pre class="code" set:html={highlightHtml(inline)} />

    <h2 id="sprite">The sprite</h2>
    <p>
      Most people never need this. Inline SVG or a framework component is simpler, and that's what the icon pages give
      you. The sprite pays off when one plain HTML page shows a lot of icons, like a toolbar, a long menu or a
      dashboard. The browser downloads every icon once as one small file and caches it, and each icon in your markup
      shrinks to a single <code>&lt;use&gt;</code> line instead of a full path.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>sprite.svg</code> holds every icon as a <code>&lt;symbol&gt;</code>. Point a <code>&lt;use&gt;</code> at
      the icon you want and set the stroke on the outer <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code>, since the symbols leave the stroke
      width to you. Host the file on your own site: browsers block <code>&lt;use&gt;</code> from pulling it off another
      domain.
    </p>
    <pre class="code" set:html={highlightHtml(sprite)} />
    <p class="sprite-get">
      <a class="btn sk btn-ink" href="/sprite.svg" download>
        <Icon name="download" size={18} plain />
        Download sprite.svg
      </a>
      <span class="hand text-xl">opened on its own it looks blank. Symbols only draw when a page uses them.</span>
    </p>

    <h2>As an image</h2>
    <p>
      Each icon is also a file at <code>/svg/&lt;name&gt;.svg</code>, for example <a href="/svg/heart.svg">heart.svg</a>.
      An <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> draws it in black: <code>currentColor</code> only works when the SVG is inline. To get
      another colour, copy the icon with that colour from its page, or download it as SVG or PNG.
    </p>
    <pre class="code" set:html={highlightHtml(img)} />

    <h2 id="wobble">The wobble</h2>
    <p>
      <Icon name="sparkle" size={22} plain boil="sm" class="mr-1.5 inline align-[-4px]" />
      The shimmer you see on this site works on your pages too. Add the helper once, then give an icon <code>zi-boil-sm</code> (14–24 px) or a big drawing <code>zi-boil</code>.
    </p>
    <pre class="code" set:html={highlightHtml(wobbleTag)} />
    <p>
      It runs for everyone by default. To pause it for people who ask their system to reduce motion, add one attribute:
    </p>
    <pre class="code" set:html={highlightHtml(wobbleOpts)} />
    <p>Or start it yourself:</p>
    <pre class="code" set:html={highlightHtml(wobbleManual)} />
    <p>
      Rather not load a script? The <strong>+ wobble</strong> tab on every icon page gives you the filter and the CSS to
      paste in directly.
    </p>

    <h2>Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Icons next to a text label are decoration: keep <code>aria-hidden="true"</code>. An icon that stands alone, like a
      close button, needs a name on the button: <code>&lt;button aria-label="Close"&gt;</code>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .pkg {
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
  }
  .sprite-get {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  .code {
    margin: 14px 0 18px;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    word-break: break-word;
  }
</style>
